1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,957
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,687
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,497
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,897
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you!

7
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,577
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, and so elusive?

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,837
Even though it's blinding me!

11
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:55,677
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you!

13
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,577
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see!

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,980
Believe in wonder!

17
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:21,137
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:24,177
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,537
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,617
We don't want to live ordinary lives.

24
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,737
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:42,480
We live in one another.

26
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:52,920
Rumble Ball

27
00:01:56,260 --> 00:01:59,197
The effect of the rumble
ball lasts three minutes.

28
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:01,456
All the time I need to take you down.

29
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:02,680
Three minutes?

30
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:06,660
You couldn't defeat me in three
years, let alone three minutes.

31
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:09,100
Just three? Amazing.

32
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:10,510
Just three?

33
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:11,620
No way.

34
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:14,420
Well, all right.

35
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:16,677
This should be an interesting battle.

36
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:18,420
Come on, you old bat.

37
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:20,680
Let me up so I can help. Rumble!

38
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:24,020
You're no match!

39
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:25,420
Not against this!

40
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,540
Marimon Snow Melting Arrow!

41
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:36,040
Lock point! Light boost!

42
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:42,020
Huh, just a transformation, eh?

43
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:43,917
I was expecting something more.

44
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,217
All you have to show
are Devil Fruit powers.

45
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:48,217
You're a zone type, just like Dalton.

46
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:50,360
So, you're a reindeer human, huh?

47
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:51,717
Heavy point!

48
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:52,940
Wait, wait, boost.

49
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:55,820
No, I'm a human reindeer.

50
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:57,310
Same thing,

51
00:02:57,420 --> 00:02:59,077
and I know everything
there is to know about

52
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:02,042
the three form transformations
you sometimes use.

53
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:05,289
Marimo's big super
surprise Katorea hammer.

54
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:09,537
Speaking of surprises, you've
got none left to spring on me.

55
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:11,137
I've seen all your forms now.

56
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:13,377
You're nothing more than a
power fighter like Dalton.

57
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:15,280
So there's no way you can.

58
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:17,100
Jumping point, jump, boost.

59
00:03:18,660 --> 00:03:20,100
Get the jump on me!

60
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:28,280
Jeez, that guy can really jump. Whoa!

61
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:30,630
What the?

62
00:03:30,713 --> 00:03:31,557
I don't get it.

63
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:32,699
What is that form?

64
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:37,577
Wasn't this human and animal form
the little reindeer from earlier?

65
00:03:37,660 --> 00:03:38,490
What now?

66
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,700
Guard point, they're boost!

67
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:53,060
Another form?

68
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:58,140
No way!

69
00:03:58,380 --> 00:03:59,500
I hit you dead on!

70
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,060
It won't work!

71
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:03,160
How is this possible?

72
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:05,614
You zone types have a three-form limit!

73
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:06,994
What the heck are you?

74
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:09,477
The Rumble Ball is a
special pill that enhances

75
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:11,957
the power of the Devil
Fruit's transformations.

76
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:13,697
Over five long years of research,

77
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:16,197
I discovered four additional
transformation points.

78
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:19,320
A-a seven-form transformation?!

79
00:04:21,020 --> 00:04:22,079
That's impossible!

80
00:04:22,340 --> 00:04:23,458
I don't believe it!

81
00:04:24,460 --> 00:04:28,037
A talking reindeer who can
change into seven forms?!

82
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:30,473
Your friend, what's the matter with him?

83
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:34,397
There's just so much happiness of meeting
a transforming reindeer a guy can take!

84
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:35,320
You bastard!

85
00:04:35,660 --> 00:04:38,260
Did you forget about fighting me?!

86
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:42,256
I won't be deceived by what
has to be an obvious sham!

87
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:43,820
It's not one!

88
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:51,700
Arm point, arm boost!

89
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:10,037
If you thought that was something,

90
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:13,296
you should see what my iron
hose can do against rocks.

91
00:05:15,260 --> 00:05:17,700
Not my hammers! What nerf!

92
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:21,700
These'll teach you...

93
00:05:22,820 --> 00:05:25,880
Barmo's Super Surprise Katorea Axe!

94
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:28,980
Snow-Splitting Flame!

95
00:05:34,180 --> 00:05:37,600
Wow, damn, that reindeer
can really take a hit.

96
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:41,200
Damn, you dodged it!

97
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:44,740
Let's see you dodge! Yes!

98
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:48,480
I'm the directional soul splitter!

99
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:01,600
You're gonna take me down, huh?

100
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:04,133
You're not fighting, you're just dosing!

101
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:15,300
Brain point, brain boost!

102
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:18,740
I wasn't just dodging your swings.

103
00:06:20,340 --> 00:06:23,380
I was looking for your weak spot. What?

104
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:25,940
This'll finish you. Skull!

105
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:35,540
A beam!

106
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:36,957
He's gonna shoot a beam!

107
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:38,377
No he won't, you idiot!

108
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:39,657
Hey, you shut your trap!

109
00:06:39,740 --> 00:06:41,857
I'm telling you, it's gotta be a beam!

110
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:43,497
How do you know that, huh, Mr.

111
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:44,410
Smart Guy?

112
00:06:44,493 --> 00:06:45,323
I just do!

113
00:06:45,406 --> 00:06:46,680
Fine, what kind of beam?

114
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:47,670
A ginormous beam!

115
00:06:47,753 --> 00:06:48,973
The castle's unguarded.

116
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:50,885
Looking for my weak spot, huh?

117
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:53,041
Well, I've got some news for you!

118
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,300
I don't have one!

119
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:04,277
Your little transforming parlor
tricks can't save you now!

120
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:08,595
And as you're about to find out,
you're the one who's gonna be finished!

121
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:11,080
Found it!

122
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:13,570
His jaw!

123
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:29,980
Where'd he go?

124
00:07:32,740 --> 00:07:33,570
A friend?

125
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:44,110
Race!

126
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:00,320
Three minutes.

127
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:04,900
Yeah! All right! Wow! Hey, Luffy.

128
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:08,157
Yeah? Where is he? Where's who?

129
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:10,740
That tin-plated bastard, he's not here!

130
00:08:15,420 --> 00:08:20,126
Well since his hippo got knocked away, I
doubt he could have snuck off very far.

131
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:22,380
Yeah, but how? When'd he go?

132
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:25,877
Probably when you were drooling
over those transformations!

133
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:26,790
How sneaky!

134
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:28,937
I'll find him!

135
00:08:29,020 --> 00:08:30,961
Where do you think he ran off to?

136
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:33,791
There's not much up here, just the castle.

137
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:36,080
And Nami's all alone in there!

138
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:41,277
If he lays a finger on her, I'll chop
him up and feed him to the sharks!

139
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,190
Hold it!

140
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:43,990
Oh, well.

141
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:46,733
I guess the nincompoop has a death wish.

142
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:51,110
What?

143
00:08:51,193 --> 00:08:52,819
I go away and this is what happens?

144
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:55,520
Drunk Castle used to be a stately palace!

145
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,217
Now it's nothing but a run-down
hobble filled with snow!

146
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:01,700
What did they do to it?

147
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:04,713
Oh, I won't let them get away with this.

148
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:09,254
I'll chew them up until there's
absolutely nothing left!

149
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:16,440
We've gotta get Vivi home.

150
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:18,397
I've spent enough time resting.

151
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:23,362
Doctorine doesn't seem to be around, so
maybe I can slip away without her noticing.

152
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:28,470
Great.

153
00:09:28,553 --> 00:09:30,065
Looks like the coast is clear.

154
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,900
What? What the? Who's he?

155
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:39,612
Well, well, another Straw Hat, I presume.

156
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:43,040
Uh-oh, he doesn't look friendly.

157
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:46,390
Huh?

158
00:09:46,473 --> 00:09:47,303
Straw Hat?

159
00:09:47,386 --> 00:09:48,216
What's that mean?

160
00:09:48,299 --> 00:09:50,597
I'm sorry, sir, but I don't
know what you're talking about.

161
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:51,510
What?

162
00:09:51,593 --> 00:09:53,180
Oh, I was wrong?

163
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:56,937
Yes, I'm just a traveler who is passing
through, and I'm actually on my way out.

164
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:57,980
Oh, I see.

165
00:09:58,520 --> 00:09:59,597
Nice talking to you.

166
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:00,880
See ya. Right.

167
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:06,530
Liar!

168
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:10,804
The king of this country
commands you to starve!

169
00:10:12,140 --> 00:10:13,260
No, I won't!

170
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:15,242
Get away from me, you big creep!

171
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:26,980
I must have gained weight recently.

172
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:28,580
Well, I can fix that.

173
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:30,096
Much, much, factory!

174
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:39,280
Uh, what is he?

175
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:53,500
He turned into a bucket?

176
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:59,280
Ah, my miraculous bone structure
shaping technique is now complete!

177
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:07,220
I'm leanin' mean!

178
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:10,540
I'm hungry.

179
00:11:19,260 --> 00:11:22,000
Time to gobble you up, Straw Hat. Ah!

180
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:23,900
Found you! Huh?

181
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:35,220
Hey, that's funny.

182
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:37,281
Wasn't that guy Big Fatso before?

183
00:11:41,420 --> 00:11:42,250
So,

184
00:11:42,333 --> 00:11:44,117
do you mind telling me
why the coat I kindly

185
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:46,906
loaned you is all torn
up before I murder you?

186
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:50,177
Do you have any idea how
much I paid for that thing?

187
00:11:50,260 --> 00:11:52,380
28,800 berries!

188
00:11:52,640 --> 00:11:53,937
That was after hackling!

189
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:55,937
Hey, wait, I didn't do it!

190
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:57,785
That loudmouth over there did!

191
00:11:58,180 --> 00:12:00,592
It's not my fault he shot a cannon at me!

192
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:04,697
Okay, then in that case, Luffy,
I guess I can forgive you.

193
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:05,610
To be honest,

194
00:12:05,693 --> 00:12:07,057
I should have known that
you would have never brought

195
00:12:07,140 --> 00:12:09,877
it back in good condition
when I let you borrow it.

196
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:16,860
You can just pay me back at my usual 300
% interest, which comes to 100,000. Ah!

197
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:18,257
You should have said!

198
00:12:18,340 --> 00:12:20,281
I would never have taken it then!

199
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:24,150
Hello!

200
00:12:24,233 --> 00:12:25,063
I'm still here!

201
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:28,065
Oh, that's right, I still
gotta kick your butt!

202
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:30,750
Ha!

203
00:12:30,833 --> 00:12:32,737
I'll be the one doing the butt-kicking!

204
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:36,537
Behind me lies this castle's arsenal, and
I'm the only one who has the key to it!

205
00:12:36,620 --> 00:12:39,837
Inside its walls are some of the
most fearsome weapons known to man!

206
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:42,640
All I need to do is
devour them Straw Hats!

207
00:12:42,820 --> 00:12:45,677
Then my munch-munch shock will
make them part of my body!

208
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:47,757
and you'll be forced to
face a fearsome living

209
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:50,037
weapon the likes of
which you've never seen!

210
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:52,238
The two of you don't stand a chance!

211
00:12:56,260 --> 00:13:00,280
I hope you're ready to die, Straw
Hats, because I'm going... Hey.

212
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:03,190
Huh?

213
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:11,640
This isn't over!

214
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:14,400
Hey, he's getting away! Come back!

215
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:18,256
At least I've got another trump card!

216
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:23,077
This must be the key to the
arsenal he was yapping about.

217
00:13:23,160 --> 00:13:26,297
Geez, why couldn't it have been the
key to this castle's treasure vault?

218
00:13:26,380 --> 00:13:27,210
Oh, man.

219
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:28,700
Nami, my love!

220
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:30,440
Thank heavens!

221
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:32,200
I'm glad you're safe!

222
00:13:33,820 --> 00:13:34,857
Sanji, what happened?

223
00:13:34,940 --> 00:13:36,017
Why are you crawling?

224
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:36,930
Are you okay?

225
00:13:37,820 --> 00:13:40,117
I'm great now that I've
seen you, Nami dear,

226
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:42,397
but there are two things that'll
make me feel even better.

227
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:45,460
If I could just rest my
head on your warm billowy.

228
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:47,060
No way!

229
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:49,620
Ready, please?

230
00:13:50,740 --> 00:13:52,020
Run all you want!

231
00:13:52,140 --> 00:13:55,022
You can't get away from
me, you stupid loudmouth!

232
00:13:55,920 --> 00:13:58,214
The upper levels are full of snow, too?

233
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:00,797
Trash my castle and defy
my orders, will they?

234
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:02,197
They won't get away with this.

235
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:05,515
It's time I taught those in
support, and it's a lesson!

236
00:14:07,340 --> 00:14:08,780
A painful lesson!

237
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:13,041
To do so, I'll use the ultimate
weapon of the entire Trump Kingdom!

238
00:14:15,620 --> 00:14:17,497
My devastatingly lethal.

239
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:19,017
Tin Titan Royal Crown?

240
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:20,380
Seven Barrel Cannon!

241
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:26,540
Oh yeah?

242
00:14:26,700 --> 00:14:28,017
Well, I've got you cornered!

243
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:30,340
On the contrary, Rubberman!

244
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:31,680
Time to die!

245
00:15:04,460 --> 00:15:05,840
Snowbird's cool!

246
00:15:11,420 --> 00:15:12,250
Stop it!

247
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:14,600
How dare you laugh at me! Shut up!

248
00:15:16,780 --> 00:15:18,420
Dr. Ean. Hmm?

249
00:15:19,980 --> 00:15:20,820
That guy.

250
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:22,060
Did you hear him?

251
00:15:24,660 --> 00:15:26,300
He called me his friend.

252
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:32,317
I have to admit I was skeptical when I
heard about this ropeway to the castle.

253
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:35,224
But here it is, just like
the young man told us.

254
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:36,877
This place looks familiar.

255
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:37,997
Didn't it used to be Dr.

256
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:38,962
Correa's house?

257
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:46,162
Great view from this thing, huh?

258
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:48,957
Yeah, but isn't it just the
teensiest bit overcrowded?

259
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:51,357
We can't let Dalton go
alone when he's injured.

260
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:52,737
We'll fight alongside him.

261
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:53,777
Okay, I get it.

262
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:57,213
But we're so overloaded, it'll
take forever to get there.

263
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:00,890
You!

264
00:16:00,973 --> 00:16:02,073
You gotta pedal faster!

265
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:04,440
Dalton, please just relax.

266
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:08,940
Wapol, who do you think you are, Dalton?

267
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:14,282
There's no medicine that
can cure fools, you say?

268
00:16:16,180 --> 00:16:18,420
Did you call me the king a fool?

269
00:16:19,480 --> 00:16:23,757
What, do you think you're some hero who
speaks for the lowly subjects of my kingdom?

270
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:24,997
Don't make me laugh!

271
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:26,374
You're just a servant!

272
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:32,177
A week in this cell will give you plenty
of time to reflect on your mistake.

273
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:34,877
There's nothing like prison
to change a man's attitude.

274
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:36,477
And just in case that doesn't work,

275
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:40,031
I'm going to have that rebellious
streak beaten out of you!

276
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:44,757
You're an excellent
god the citizens trust.

277
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:45,781
Don't be a fool.

278
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:49,160
Apologize to the king and
show him respect, Dalton.

279
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:52,240
That dead Dr.

280
00:16:52,380 --> 00:16:53,437
Hiriluk was an idiot.

281
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:55,517
I can't believe you fell for his nonsense.

282
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:57,657
Risking your status
and insulting the king?

283
00:16:57,740 --> 00:16:59,622
Have you lost your mind, Dalton?

284
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:02,376
I'll grant you a full pardon, Dalton.

285
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:06,482
All you have to do is get on your
knees and say they're following.

286
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:09,337
I'm so sorry, oh great King Wiper.

287
00:17:09,420 --> 00:17:12,126
You always know what's
right for this country!

288
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:19,340
To hell with status!

289
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:21,380
To hell with the king!

290
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:26,440
You dare mock me too, stupid bird!

291
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:27,895
I'm the king of drum!

292
00:17:32,060 --> 00:17:33,300
Yeah, so what?

293
00:17:33,860 --> 00:17:37,657
It doesn't matter if you're a
king, or even if you're a god!

294
00:17:37,740 --> 00:17:42,780
It doesn't matter if you're someone who's
great or someone who's not so great.

295
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:45,376
I'm still gonna kick your lousy butt.

296
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:48,940
It does matter, Straw Hat.

297
00:17:49,220 --> 00:17:51,357
Trump Kingdom is a member
of the world government.

298
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:53,264
Don't you know what that means?

299
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:57,220
It means this is a capital
offense because I'm the king!

300
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,471
Like I said, Big Mouth, it doesn't matter.

301
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:03,016
King or no king, I'm taking you down.

302
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:05,660
Oh, really?

303
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:07,057
Well, not if I...

304
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:09,280
Take you down first, Strowhand!

305
00:18:10,780 --> 00:18:12,400
That won't work.

306
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:16,120
But this will much,
much shock Tang Cannon!

307
00:18:17,020 --> 00:18:19,940
Ah, his tongue turned
into a cannon! Goodbye!

308
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:38,870
Dalton!

309
00:18:38,953 --> 00:18:40,071
Someone help me lift him!

310
00:18:40,180 --> 00:18:42,120
Dalton, can you hear me? Dalton!

311
00:18:44,220 --> 00:18:45,100
I'm okay.

312
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:50,000
Please don't die!

313
00:18:56,020 --> 00:18:56,980
I won't.

314
00:18:57,240 --> 00:18:58,260
I can't.

315
00:18:58,600 --> 00:19:02,600
Not until I put an end to Wobble
and what he's done to this country!

316
00:19:02,700 --> 00:19:06,057
A government should care about
its country and its people.

317
00:19:06,140 --> 00:19:07,697
You mean you weren't joking?

318
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:09,956
That's what you really think, Dalton?

319
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:13,757
Please, a government doesn't
need to have a heart.

320
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:14,670
That's right.

321
00:19:14,753 --> 00:19:16,778
It just needs to control the people.

322
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:26,320
What are you doing? Unhand me!

323
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,260
Stop it! Let me go!

324
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:30,457
You can't do this!

325
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:32,597
I have patients who will
die if I don't treat them!

326
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:34,033
Throw him in the ocean!

327
00:19:34,220 --> 00:19:36,797
If he resists, you have my
permission to shoot him!

328
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:37,710
No!

329
00:19:37,793 --> 00:19:39,497
Think of my patients at least!

330
00:19:39,580 --> 00:19:41,317
They're the ones who are going to suffer!

331
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,460
Don't do this!

332
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:47,720
To hell with controlling the country!

333
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:52,470
God.

334
00:19:53,380 --> 00:19:54,909
And none of them are sick.

335
00:19:58,300 --> 00:20:01,947
Show them what happens to a
country that doesn't have a heart!

336
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:13,910
dynamite.

337
00:20:13,993 --> 00:20:15,817
everyone listen!

338
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:16,797
once we arrive.

339
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:17,757
take cover.

340
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:19,017
because once I'm inside.

341
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:20,453
there'll be explosions.

342
00:20:24,980 --> 00:20:26,157
that idiot!

343
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:27,800
he let his guard down.

344
00:20:30,660 --> 00:20:32,920
pollock is talking. Huh?

345
00:20:33,140 --> 00:20:34,817
One, two...

346
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:36,860
Hey, what are you doing?

347
00:20:37,280 --> 00:20:38,120
That!

348
00:20:38,560 --> 00:20:39,620
No, stop!

349
00:20:40,100 --> 00:20:41,000
Go, go!

350
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:43,837
Go, go!

351
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:45,120
Go, go, go!

352
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:01,750
Dr.

353
00:21:01,833 --> 00:21:06,280
Rain, it certainly seems
like it's finally over.

354
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:14,580
I told you not to mess with that flag.

355
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:15,570
Now I'm sorry.

356
00:21:15,653 --> 00:21:17,218
I'm finally going to kick your butt!

357
00:21:21,580 --> 00:21:22,410
Doctor...

358
00:21:23,220 --> 00:21:24,140
Wait a minute!

359
00:21:24,420 --> 00:21:26,714
I'll give you a battle of the position!

360
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:30,200
Look, there's something going
on on top of the castle!

361
00:21:36,820 --> 00:21:37,650
Doctor...

362
00:21:41,180 --> 00:21:42,010
This...

363
00:21:42,093 --> 00:21:43,220
This kingdom...

364
00:21:44,220 --> 00:21:46,220
Drum Kingdom, it's...

365
00:21:50,940 --> 00:21:51,980
Fine!

366
00:21:52,420 --> 00:21:53,832
I'll make you vice king!

367
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:56,100
It's about to fall!

368
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:57,980
Bazooka!

369
00:22:18,520 --> 00:22:23,120
So the Drum Kingdom was ultimately
defeated by the Skull and Crossbones.

370
00:22:39,660 --> 00:22:40,900
Everybody, wait here.

371
00:22:41,060 --> 00:22:45,178
I'll brave whatever dangers lie ahead
and let you know when it's safe.

372
00:22:47,520 --> 00:22:48,540
I'm going first.

373
00:22:59,780 --> 00:23:01,717
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

374
00:23:01,800 --> 00:23:02,917
Just watching your back.

375
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,637
Hiding behind it from one like it?

376
00:23:04,720 --> 00:23:07,073
Why'd you even come if you're so scared?

377
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:08,150
Scared?

378
00:23:08,233 --> 00:23:09,063
Don't be ridiculous.

379
00:23:09,146 --> 00:23:11,256
I always laugh at the face of danger.

380
00:23:13,820 --> 00:23:14,650
Luffy!

381
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:17,230
Who's up?

382
00:23:29,580 --> 00:23:31,380
Why'd you do that, you moron?

383
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:33,600
I didn't recognize you at first.

384
00:23:34,820 --> 00:23:37,777
I thought you were more of Big
Mouse guards coming to fight.

385
00:23:37,860 --> 00:23:40,257
Wow, I'm really surprised you
guys came all the way up here.

386
00:23:40,340 --> 00:23:43,180
Well, not you, Zoro, but you, Usopp.

387
00:23:43,560 --> 00:23:46,537
Aren't you normally scared of doing
stuff like climbing mountains?

388
00:23:49,060 --> 00:23:52,137
Whenever there's a towering peak
in front of me, I get to climbing.

389
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:56,277
But let me tell you, scaling that
mountain hand over hand was no picnic!

390
00:23:56,360 --> 00:23:59,125
Actually, we took a
ropeway car up here, Luffy.

391
00:23:59,500 --> 00:24:02,300
Nami and Sanji, are they all right? Yeah!

392
00:24:02,620 --> 00:24:04,208
Both of them are just fine!

393
00:24:04,380 --> 00:24:07,697
I just have to say, we took a
ropeway car, but let me tell you,

394
00:24:07,780 --> 00:24:09,300
taking it was no picnic!

395
00:24:09,840 --> 00:24:10,670
Here's why.

396
00:24:10,820 --> 00:24:15,640
We were on the way, then a giant condor
flew out of nowhere and attacked us.

397
00:24:15,740 --> 00:24:19,737
So, what was that you were doing on
top of the castle a few minutes ago?

398
00:24:19,820 --> 00:24:21,761
Beating the crap out of the king.

399
00:24:22,560 --> 00:24:23,390
Oh. Okay.

400
00:24:23,780 --> 00:24:27,577
You mean that person I saw flying
through the air was actually Wapol?

401
00:24:27,660 --> 00:24:28,960
You beat him?

402
00:24:29,280 --> 00:24:30,537
Yep, I sure did.

403
00:24:30,620 --> 00:24:33,197
I threw a rope around his neck
and showed that bird who was boss.

404
00:24:33,280 --> 00:24:34,110
Me, Captain Step!

405
00:24:34,193 --> 00:24:36,177
And his two henchmen,
what happened to them?

406
00:24:36,260 --> 00:24:37,857
Oh, well, the reindeer beat them up.

407
00:24:37,940 --> 00:24:40,380
What? Those two? A reindeer?

408
00:24:40,760 --> 00:24:42,177
Once again, Captain Usopp!

409
00:24:42,260 --> 00:24:43,240
Oh, hey, Usopp!

410
00:24:43,380 --> 00:24:44,417
I made a new friend!

411
00:24:44,500 --> 00:24:45,457
And you gotta meet him!

412
00:24:45,540 --> 00:24:46,370
Get this!

413
00:24:46,453 --> 00:24:47,283
He's a reindeer!

414
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:49,190
Reindeer?

415
00:24:52,500 --> 00:24:53,620
A reindeer...

416
00:25:01,420 --> 00:25:02,940
It is you...

417
00:25:05,040 --> 00:25:05,870
STOP!

418
00:25:06,260 --> 00:25:10,260
I apologize for those who had the
nerve to laugh at Heraluk's death.

419
00:25:11,440 --> 00:25:14,264
Without enough strength,
you'd only die in vain.

420
00:25:17,540 --> 00:25:19,080
Don't waste your life.

421
00:25:19,940 --> 00:25:22,240
Don't sacrifice it for this country.

422
00:25:25,260 --> 00:25:29,120
Blue Nose, you never gave up, did you?

423
00:25:29,580 --> 00:25:33,760
You still kept fighting, believing
in what this country could become.

424
00:25:42,820 --> 00:25:47,640
And now, thanks to you, Drum
Kingdom, it can finally be reborn.

425
00:25:57,540 --> 00:25:58,370
What?

426
00:25:58,453 --> 00:26:00,717
What is that strange
creature behind that tree?

427
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:02,697
It almost looks like a reindeer.

428
00:26:02,780 --> 00:26:04,880
No, you're wrong.

429
00:26:05,040 --> 00:26:06,220
It's a monster.

430
00:26:06,780 --> 00:26:08,400
No, don't shoot him!

431
00:26:09,420 --> 00:26:11,240
It's a Yeti! No!

432
00:26:11,860 --> 00:26:13,240
Somebody shoot him!

433
00:26:16,800 --> 00:26:17,680
Jerk face!

434
00:26:17,960 --> 00:26:19,548
He's not a Yeti, you idiot!

435
00:26:19,820 --> 00:26:20,938
He's my new friend!

436
00:26:21,140 --> 00:26:22,437
That thing's your friend?

437
00:26:22,520 --> 00:26:24,873
You guys scared him so bad, he ran away!

438
00:26:26,060 --> 00:26:28,837
I'll bring him back so you
can meet him, you jerks!

439
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:29,750
Hey!

440
00:26:29,833 --> 00:26:33,132
Come back reindeer, I want to
introduce you to my friends!

441
00:26:33,320 --> 00:26:35,457
I'm going to stop running for a second!

442
00:26:35,540 --> 00:26:37,257
But my friends wouldn't meet you!

443
00:26:37,340 --> 00:26:38,477
You wouldn't shoot me!

444
00:26:38,560 --> 00:26:40,972
That's just because I don't know you yet!

445
00:26:41,220 --> 00:26:42,320
Hey, slow down!

446
00:26:42,600 --> 00:26:43,776
Where are you going?

447
00:26:43,880 --> 00:26:46,557
My friends are back that way,
don't you want to meet us?

448
00:26:46,640 --> 00:26:49,417
Doctor, this is for the best, isn't it?

449
00:26:49,500 --> 00:26:51,237
They're not so bad, you'll see!

450
00:26:51,320 --> 00:26:53,908
Come back and meet them,
they're my friends!

451
00:26:54,140 --> 00:26:56,787
My friends like yours,
I don't need anything!

452
00:27:01,240 --> 00:27:03,887
Are you sure you're
going to be okay, Dalton?

453
00:27:04,180 --> 00:27:05,300
Yes, I'm fine.

454
00:27:05,700 --> 00:27:07,857
Just feeling a little drained, that's all.

455
00:27:07,940 --> 00:27:08,770
Hey!

456
00:27:08,853 --> 00:27:09,683
You over there!

457
00:27:12,180 --> 00:27:13,600
Dr. Kureha!

458
00:27:16,220 --> 00:27:18,044
Yeah, it's good to see you too.

459
00:27:18,440 --> 00:27:21,911
Now be useful and take the
injured guy to the medical ward.

460
00:27:22,200 --> 00:27:25,257
Nami, you really should stay and
have your illness completely treated.

461
00:27:25,340 --> 00:27:26,400
Be quiet.

462
00:27:26,660 --> 00:27:30,957
If I don't escape from here now, we won't
be able to set sail for two more days.

463
00:27:31,040 --> 00:27:32,577
You know how worried Vivi is.

464
00:27:32,660 --> 00:27:34,017
We need to get her to Alabax.

465
00:27:34,100 --> 00:27:37,177
Quit all this grumbling and
get back to the medical ward.

466
00:27:37,260 --> 00:27:38,090
Move it!

467
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:39,620
Right now!

468
00:27:56,660 --> 00:28:01,420
Just as I expected, his injuries have
gotten worse due to overexertion.

469
00:28:06,520 --> 00:28:07,480
Much better.

470
00:28:08,620 --> 00:28:12,300
Dalton, surely you would know
where the key to the arsenal is.

471
00:28:12,480 --> 00:28:13,480
Isn't that right?

472
00:28:14,460 --> 00:28:15,360
The arsenal?

473
00:28:15,620 --> 00:28:17,502
Why do you need to get in there?

474
00:28:17,680 --> 00:28:20,277
That's really none of
your business, now, is it?

475
00:28:20,360 --> 00:28:23,597
Wapol always carried that key with
him to keep it secure, he said.

476
00:28:23,680 --> 00:28:27,837
In which case, the key was likely
blown into the sky with him Oh, really?

477
00:28:27,920 --> 00:28:28,750
Is that so?

478
00:28:28,880 --> 00:28:30,880
Well, that's a shame Dr.

479
00:28:31,040 --> 00:28:31,870
Ean

480
00:28:32,260 --> 00:28:35,237
Think we can talk about your
fee for treating our crew?

481
00:28:35,320 --> 00:28:36,438
Could you waive it?

482
00:28:36,540 --> 00:28:40,187
Oh, and could you go ahead and
discharge me right now as well?

483
00:28:40,940 --> 00:28:41,937
Is that a joke?

484
00:28:42,020 --> 00:28:44,117
Because you should know better
than that by now, girly?

485
00:28:44,200 --> 00:28:45,600
For my medical fee,

486
00:28:45,740 --> 00:28:49,117
I will be taking all of the cargo and
money you have on that ship of yours!

487
00:28:49,200 --> 00:28:52,318
And you will stay here and
recover for two more days.

488
00:28:53,200 --> 00:28:54,557
Nami, she's right, you know.

489
00:28:54,640 --> 00:28:56,317
You need to complete your treatment.

490
00:28:56,400 --> 00:28:57,230
I'm fine.

491
00:28:57,313 --> 00:28:58,857
I don't even feel like
I'm going to die anymore.

492
00:28:58,940 --> 00:29:01,528
That isn't exactly a
very convincing reason.

493
00:29:05,620 --> 00:29:07,060
The key to the arsenal.

494
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:09,205
This is what you needed, yeah?

495
00:29:10,800 --> 00:29:12,577
How did you end up with that key?

496
00:29:12,660 --> 00:29:15,817
If that's truly the real one,
how'd you get a hold of it?

497
00:29:15,900 --> 00:29:16,800
I stole it.

498
00:29:17,760 --> 00:29:21,137
You've certainly got some guts trying
to negotiate with me like this.

499
00:29:21,220 --> 00:29:25,044
You really are an unbelievably
frustrating little girl, you know.

500
00:29:26,020 --> 00:29:26,850
Okay, then.

501
00:29:27,220 --> 00:29:30,957
You don't have to pay my doctor's fee,
but that's as much as I'll agree to.

502
00:29:31,040 --> 00:29:33,997
As a doctor, I can't allow you
to leave in good conscience.

503
00:29:34,080 --> 00:29:35,080
Not for two days.

504
00:29:35,180 --> 00:29:36,010
Wait a second.

505
00:29:36,100 --> 00:29:38,117
In that case, I'm afraid
we don't have a deal.

506
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:39,030
Give it back.

507
00:29:39,300 --> 00:29:40,640
Listen here, girl.

508
00:29:41,940 --> 00:29:45,377
I have to leave you alone now
and go take care of a few things.

509
00:29:45,460 --> 00:29:49,217
If you look in the back room, you might
find a dresser with one of my coats in it.

510
00:29:49,300 --> 00:29:52,097
And it's not exactly like I'm
posting any guards on you.

511
00:29:52,180 --> 00:29:56,277
Also, the young man with the spinal fissure
should be well enough to travel by now.

512
00:29:56,360 --> 00:29:59,595
But, girl, don't you even
think about trying to escape.

513
00:29:59,740 --> 00:30:01,360
You guys, come with me.

514
00:30:01,520 --> 00:30:03,197
I have some heavy lifting for you to do.

515
00:30:03,280 --> 00:30:04,221
Okay, all right.

516
00:30:11,440 --> 00:30:15,457
Did she really just tell us to steal
her coat, get Sanji, and sneak out?

517
00:30:15,540 --> 00:30:16,620
I think so.

518
00:30:17,040 --> 00:30:19,040
That's what it sounded like to me.

519
00:30:25,500 --> 00:30:27,800
I sure have been running a long time.

520
00:30:28,080 --> 00:30:29,962
Night came before I realized it.

521
00:30:30,440 --> 00:30:32,616
I don't hear that rubber guy anymore.

522
00:30:32,740 --> 00:30:35,093
Looks like I finally shook him, I guess.

523
00:30:35,980 --> 00:30:37,360
This is for the best.

524
00:30:37,760 --> 00:30:39,340
I can't leave this place.

525
00:30:39,540 --> 00:30:40,400
I just can't.

526
00:30:42,040 --> 00:30:43,864
Looks like a full moon tonight.

527
00:30:45,220 --> 00:30:46,240
Hey, dear!

528
00:30:48,780 --> 00:30:50,120
I can't believe it.

529
00:30:50,380 --> 00:30:52,417
Those guys are still looking for me?

530
00:30:52,500 --> 00:30:53,382
Come on, Luffy.

531
00:30:53,600 --> 00:30:55,017
Why don't you just give it up?

532
00:30:55,100 --> 00:30:58,097
We've been tracking him forever,
and he still hasn't shown up.

533
00:30:58,180 --> 00:31:00,117
He's not interested in becoming a pirate.

534
00:31:00,200 --> 00:31:01,697
You're just going to have to accept that.

535
00:31:01,780 --> 00:31:03,000
No, that's not true.

536
00:31:03,260 --> 00:31:05,617
I want the reindeer to
be a pirate with us.

537
00:31:05,700 --> 00:31:09,177
Just because you want something
doesn't mean it's going to happen.

538
00:31:09,260 --> 00:31:11,789
It's not that I don't
want to go with them.

539
00:31:12,100 --> 00:31:12,930
Reindeer!

540
00:31:13,360 --> 00:31:14,190
Reindeer!

541
00:31:14,273 --> 00:31:16,900
Wherever you are, reindeer, come out!

542
00:31:17,160 --> 00:31:18,720
But I'm not going to go.

543
00:31:18,900 --> 00:31:19,800
I can't go.

544
00:31:20,100 --> 00:31:22,580
I'm nothing like them, the humans.

545
00:31:30,220 --> 00:31:31,280
Reindeer guy!

546
00:31:35,340 --> 00:31:36,170
Tony?

547
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:44,165
Hey, you're gonna come on our
ship and be a pirate with us, kay?

548
00:31:45,060 --> 00:31:45,940
I can't.

549
00:31:46,040 --> 00:31:47,417
Sure you can't, reindeer.

550
00:31:47,500 --> 00:31:48,777
It's a whole lot of fun.

551
00:31:48,860 --> 00:31:50,742
That's not a very good argument.

552
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:52,880
I can't.

553
00:31:54,500 --> 00:31:56,382
I'm not a human, I'm a reindeer!

554
00:31:56,700 --> 00:31:59,112
I have antlers and hooves, don't you see?

555
00:32:00,240 --> 00:32:01,840
I even have a blue nose!

556
00:32:03,520 --> 00:32:08,285
Now that you've heard his story, do you
think you can heal the scar on his heart?

557
00:32:09,660 --> 00:32:12,660
Okay, maybe I do want to be a pirate!

558
00:32:15,240 --> 00:32:16,937
But I can't ever be one of you!

559
00:32:17,020 --> 00:32:18,840
I'm not human! I'm a monster!

560
00:32:19,260 --> 00:32:22,417
I can't be your friend and I can't
become a pirate on your ship!

561
00:32:22,500 --> 00:32:23,330
You see?

562
00:32:24,440 --> 00:32:26,117
I'm just here to say...

563
00:32:26,200 --> 00:32:27,980
thank you.

564
00:32:28,840 --> 00:32:31,600
I appreciate you asking
me to join your ship.

565
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:34,920
That was really nice, so thank you.

566
00:32:39,080 --> 00:32:41,060
I'm going to stay here for now.

567
00:32:44,160 --> 00:32:48,260
But if you wanted to, you could
stop by here again. Shut up!

568
00:32:48,560 --> 00:32:49,880
Let's go! No!

569
00:33:02,480 --> 00:33:06,068
Most people don't make friends
by telling someone to shut up.

570
00:33:21,120 --> 00:33:23,477
My life has been too still.

571
00:33:23,560 --> 00:33:26,117
My heart is unfulfilled.

572
00:33:26,200 --> 00:33:29,940
But you could be the one to set me free.

573
00:33:31,840 --> 00:33:33,877
Something has to change.

574
00:33:33,960 --> 00:33:36,637
My world can be rearranged.

575
00:33:36,720 --> 00:33:41,780
I'll do anything as
long as you are with me.

576
00:33:42,860 --> 00:33:47,057
I've grown stronger having you by my side.

577
00:33:47,140 --> 00:33:52,300
We've started on an everlasting ride.

578
00:33:52,840 --> 00:33:57,400
I'm invincible when your love is near.

579
00:33:57,960 --> 00:34:02,297
When I'm with you I have no fear.

580
00:34:02,380 --> 00:34:08,857
Let's see how far we can make this go.

581
00:34:08,940 --> 00:34:12,157
The world is ours.

582
00:34:12,240 --> 00:34:14,137
You're just right, I know.

583
00:34:14,220 --> 00:34:18,677
I see it shine in the distance.

584
00:34:18,760 --> 00:34:24,620
Glistening like water when
the sun Rises in the dawn.
